IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sge-p10a-362`

-- Tests of s 362 (Part 10A, Transfer of registration: revocation). Every expected value is written from the text, beside the assertion,
-- before the run. Hand-counted dates: 1 March 2027 plus 30 days is 31 March 2027, plus 45 days is 15 April 2027.

§ `Section 362(1): the Registrar may revoke`

#ASSERT `s 362(1) the Registrar may by order revoke the registration of the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The company has not failed to comply with s 359(6): the grant's "if" gate failed; the text says nothing more.
#ASSERT `s 362(1) the Registrar may by order revoke the registration of the company` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 362(2): what the Registrar must do before making an order`

#ASSERT `s 362(2)(a) the Registrar has given the company written notice of the intention to revoke the registration` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(2)(a) the Registrar has given the company written notice of the intention to revoke the registration` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) "a period of at least 30 days": 29 is short, 30 and more are enough.
#ASSERT `s 362(2)(b) the notice specifies a period of at least 30 days for written representations` 29 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(2)(b) the notice specifies a period of at least 30 days for written representations` 30 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(2)(b) the notice specifies a period of at least 30 days for written representations` 31 EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) "(if any)": representations received in time and considered; or none received; or received and not considered.
#ASSERT `s 362(2)(c) the Registrar has considered the company's written representations` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(2)(c) the Registrar has considered the company's written representations` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(2)(c) the Registrar has considered the company's written representations` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The subsection. Arguments: notice given; days specified; representations received in time; considered them.
#ASSERT `s 362(2) the Registrar has done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` TRUE 30 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(2) the Registrar has done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` TRUE 45 TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(2) the Registrar has done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` FALSE 30 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(2) the Registrar has done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` TRUE 29 FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(2) the Registrar has done what the subsection requires before making an order of revocation` TRUE 30 TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The Registrar's duties as a rule: notice, then consideration. Both done: fulfilled. Only the notice: the second duty stands.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 362(2) before making an order of revocation the Registrar must give notice and consider representations` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 362(2)(a) and (b) give the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke the registration, specifying a period of at least 30 days for written representations` AT 1
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 362(2)(c) consider the company's written representations` AT 40

-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 362(2) before making an order of revocation the Registrar must give notice and consider representations` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 362(2)(a) and (b) give the company written notice of the Registrar's intention to revoke the registration, specifying a period of at least 30 days for written representations` AT 1

-- The company's right to make representations within the period the notice specifies (30 days here): day 30 is in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 362(2)(b) the company may make written representations within the period the notice specifies` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme Pte. Ltd." DOES `s 362(2)(b) make written representations to the Registrar` AT 30

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 362(2)(b) the company may make written representations within the period the notice specifies` "Acme Pte. Ltd." 30 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 31

§ `Section 362(3): the order`

-- Arguments: the date the notice was given; the days it specifies; the date of the order; cause to the contrary shown.
-- 30 days from 1 March 2027 end on 31 March 2027: an order on that day is not "at the expiration"; the next day it is.
#ASSERT `s 362(3) the Registrar may order that the registration of the company be revoked` (Date 1 3 2027) 30 (Date 31 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(3) the Registrar may order that the registration of the company be revoked` (Date 1 3 2027) 30 (Date 1 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless cause to the contrary is previously shown": shown, so no order.
#ASSERT `s 362(3) the Registrar may order that the registration of the company be revoked` (Date 1 3 2027) 30 (Date 1 4 2027) TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A longer period (45 days, ending 15 April 2027) is the time mentioned in the notice.
#ASSERT `s 362(3) the Registrar may order that the registration of the company be revoked` (Date 1 3 2027) 45 (Date 15 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(3) the Registrar may order that the registration of the company be revoked` (Date 1 3 2027) 45 (Date 16 4 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A notice naming 29 days is not the notice mentioned in subsection (2): no power, even long after.
#ASSERT `s 362(3) the Registrar may order that the registration of the company be revoked` (Date 1 3 2027) 29 (Date 1 6 2027) FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 362(4): after the order`

#ASSERT `s 362(4)(a) the Registrar has caused a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(4)(a) the Registrar has caused a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(4)(b) the Registrar has served a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(4)(b) the Registrar has served a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Arguments: published; served.
#ASSERT `s 362(4) the Registrar has published and served the notice of the order of revocation` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(4) the Registrar has published and served the notice of the order of revocation` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(4) the Registrar has published and served the notice of the order of revocation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 362(4) the Registrar must publish the notice of the order of revocation and serve a copy on the company` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 362(4)(a) cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette` AT 2
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 362(4)(b) serve a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company` AT 3

-- Published, not yet served: the second duty stands while the input has not run out (a trace that waits past it ends BREACH).
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 362(4) the Registrar must publish the notice of the order of revocation and serve a copy on the company` 45 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 362(4)(a) cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette` AT 2

-- late: published on day 2, served only on day 400, past the 7 days the input is for the second duty, so BREACH
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 362(4) the Registrar must publish the notice of the order of revocation and serve a copy on the company` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 362(4)(a) cause a notice of the order of revocation to be published in the Gazette` AT 2
    PARTY Registrar DOES `s 362(4)(b) serve a copy of the notice of the order of revocation on the company` AT 400

§ `Section 362(5): the order takes effect on publication`

-- Arguments: published; the date of publication; the date asked about. Published on 10 June 2027.
#ASSERT `s 362(5) the order of revocation has taken effect` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 10 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(5) the order of revocation has taken effect` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 11 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(5) the order of revocation has taken effect` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 9 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(5) the order of revocation has taken effect` FALSE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 11 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(5) the company has ceased to be a company as defined in section 4(1)` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 10 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(5) the company has ceased to be a company as defined in section 4(1)` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 9 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(5) the company has ceased to be a company as defined in section 4(1)` FALSE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 11 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(5) the provisions of this Act have ceased to apply to the company` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 10 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(5) the provisions of this Act have ceased to apply to the company` TRUE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 9 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(5) the provisions of this Act have ceased to apply to the company` FALSE (Date 10 6 2027) (Date 11 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 362(6): the order is final`

#ASSERT `s 362(6) the order of revocation is final` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(6) the order of revocation is final` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 362(7): liability continues`

-- Arguments: an order has been made; the person is an officer; the person is a member; the person has a liability in respect of the company.
#ASSERT `s 362(7) the liability of the person continues despite the order of revocation` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(7) the liability of the person continues despite the order of revocation` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 362(7) the liability of the person continues despite the order of revocation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A creditor, say: neither officer nor member. The text says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 362(7) the liability of the person continues despite the order of revocation` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- An officer with no liability: "(if any)", nothing continues and the text says nothing more.
#ASSERT `s 362(7) the liability of the person continues despite the order of revocation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- No order yet: the subsection is about the time after one.
#ASSERT `s 362(7) the liability of the person continues despite the order of revocation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 362(8): rights and claims are not prejudiced`

#ASSERT `s 362(8) section 362 prejudices the enforcement of the right or claim` `s 362(8)(a) the enforcement by a person of a right or claim against the company` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(8) section 362 prejudices the enforcement of the right or claim` `s 362(8)(b) the enforcement by the company of a right or claim against a person` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 362(8) section 362 prejudices the enforcement of the right or claim` `s 362(8) some other enforcement` EQUALS NOTHING
